{"assets":["/statement-assets/aac42da254b0db176931530d01746568ec4c212c95bc967416a2c652ac8427f5.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1575","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M. Managing Telephone Poles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mr. Chanek's city can be represented as a plane. He wants to build a housing complex in the city."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are some telephone poles on the plane, which is represented by a grid $$$a$$$ of size $$$(n + 1) \\times (m + 1)$$$. There is a telephone pole at $$$(x, y)$$$ if $$$a_{x, y} = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each point $$$(x, y)$$$, define $$$S(x, y)$$$ as the square of the Euclidean distance between the nearest pole and $$$(x, y)$$$. Formally, the square of the Euclidean distance between two points $$$(x_1, y_1)$$$ and $$$(x_2, y_2)$$$ is $$$(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To optimize the building plan, the project supervisor asks you the sum of all $$$S(x, y)$$$ for each $$$0 \\leq x \\leq n$$$ and $$$0 \\leq y \\leq m$$$. Help him by finding the value of $$$\\sum_{x=0}^{n} {\\sum_{y=0}^{m} {S(x, y)}}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$0 \\leq n, m \\lt 2000$$$) — the size of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$(n + 1)$$$ lines follow, each containing $$$(m + 1)$$$ integers $$$a_{i, j}$$$ ($$$0 \\leq a_{i, j} \\leq 1$$$) — the grid denoting the positions of telephone poles in the plane. There is at least one telephone pole in the given grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output an integer denoting the value of $$$\\sum_{x=0}^{n} {\\sum_{y=0}^{m} {S(x, y)}}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2\n101\n000\n000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n18\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 4\n10010\n00000\n01000\n00001\n00100\n00010\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n36\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/aac42da254b0db176931530d01746568ec4c212c95bc967416a2c652ac8427f5.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the nearest telephone pole for the points $$$(0,0)$$$, $$$(1,0)$$$, $$$(2,0)$$$, $$$(0,1)$$$, $$$(1,1)$$$, and $$$(2,1)$$$ is at $$$(0, 0)$$$. While the nearest telephone pole for the points $$$(0, 2)$$$, $$$(1,2)$$$, and $$$(2,2)$$$ is at $$$(0, 2)$$$. Thus, $$$\\sum_{x=0}^{n} {\\sum_{y=0}^{m} {S(x, y)}} = (0 + 1 + 4) + (1 + 2 + 5) + (0 + 1 + 4) = 18$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"M","problemCode":"1575M","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1575/problem/M"}